  "body": "PATCH `4.22.1` → `4.22.2`.\n\n## 1. Unreported caching now reads as \"—\", not \"0.0%\"\n\nA provider that never reports prompt caching rendered as **0.0%**, which looks like *caching is broken here* rather than *this upstream doesn't tell us*.\n\nThe stats now count how many requests actually carried a cache figure. The rate shows **—** when that count is zero; a provider that genuinely reports no hits still shows **0.0%**. Measured-zero stays distinguishable from unsupported.\n\n```\nreported zero     -> 0.0%\nnever reported    -> —\nreal NIM sample   -> 2.6%\n```\n\nThis matters concretely for the NIM question: NVIDIA's hosted endpoint returns a constant token or two under `prompt_tokens_details` rather than doing real prefix caching. Verified by sending the same 9,039-token prompt four times:\n\n```\ncall 1: prompt=9039  cached=16\ncall 2: prompt=9039  cached=16\ncall 3: prompt=9039  cached=16\ncall 4: prompt=9039  cached=16\n```\n\nReal prefix caching would show ~9,000 on the repeats. NVIDIA documents prefix caching as a **self-hosted** toggle (`NIM_ENABLE_KV_CACHE_REUSE=1`), not something enabled on the shared hosted endpoint — so a near-zero rate there is accurate, and our mapping is correct.\n\n## 2. `docs/USAGE.md`\n\nA complete guide covering the path a new user actually walks:\n\n- **Install** — including the reopen-your-terminal `PATH` step that trips almost everyone, and the one-environment-only warning for Windows/WSL\n- **Adding keys** — the validate-then-apply loop, and what a 401 vs 404 actually tells you\n- **Model tiers** — why the agent's picker shows FCC's catalog, and why mapping Haiku to something fast matters more than people expect\n- **Connecting Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex, Pi** — using the existing screenshots, including the Desktop developer-menu and gateway-config images\n- **Web search** — provider choice, and a full recipe for getting *full page text* instead of snippets, with the cost warning\n- **Analytics** — both stores, and how to read the token columns including what **—** means\n- **Rotation, updating** (including the deferred Windows install), **troubleshooting**\n\nLinked from the README header and after the feature table.\n\n## Verification\n\nA checker confirms every referenced asset exists and every TOC anchor resolves:\n\n```\nreferenced files missing: none\nbroken TOC anchors: none\n```\n\nNew test asserts `cache_reported` separates a silent provider from one reporting zero. Full suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe guide documents current behaviour and will drift as features change — the web search option names in particular. Nothing enforces that automatically; the `.env.example` contract test only covers the catalog, not this page.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
