     "date": "2026-08-01T11:24:59Z"
    },
    "message": "docs: add a complete usage guide, and distinguish unreported caching from 0%\n\nA provider that never reports prompt caching rendered as \"0.0%\", which reads as\n\"caching is broken here\" rather than \"this upstream does not tell us\". The\nstats now count how many requests actually carried a cache figure, and the rate\nshows an em dash when that count is zero. A provider that genuinely reports no\ncache hits still reads 0.0%, so measured-zero stays distinguishable from\nunsupported. This matters concretely: NVIDIA NIM's hosted endpoint returns a\nconstant token or two under prompt_tokens_details rather than doing real prefix\ncaching -- verified by sending the same 9k-token prompt four times and getting\ncached=16 every time -- so a near-zero rate there is accurate.\n\nThe new docs/USAGE.md covers the path a new user actually walks: install and\nthe PATH restart that trips everyone up, first run, adding and validating keys,\nmapping model tiers, connecting Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Codex and Pi with\nthe existing screenshots, web search including how to get full page text rather\nthan snippets, both analytics stores and how to read the token columns, key\nrotation, the deferred Windows update, and troubleshooting.\n\nVerified: a checker confirms every referenced asset exists and every table of\ncontents anchor resolves. Full suite passes except the 14 failures that also\nfail on unmodified main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
